In $\triangle ABC$, the sides opposite to angles $A$, $B$, and $C$ are $a$, $b$, and $c$, respectively. Given that $A > B$, $\cos C= \frac {5}{13}$, and $\cos (A-B)= \frac {3}{5}$.

(1) Find the value of $\cos 2A$;

